        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "K18",
        "text": "Rankings with potential ties (e.g., returns_pct, risk_score) must include a deterministic secondary key (e.g., ORDER BY score DESC, investor_id ASC) to ensure stable and reproducible results.",
        "fields": [],
        "citations": [],
        "sources": [
          "rules"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "K19",
        "text": "When selecting investors with the lowest scores, explicitly filter out NULL values (e.g., WHERE score IS NOT NULL) to prevent missing data from being treated as the lowest value.",
        "fields": [],
        "citations": [],
        "sources": [
          "rules"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "K20",
        "text": "When grouping by investor attributes (e.g., risk_tolerance), compute all averaged metrics per-investor first, then average across investors to maintain uniform grain.",
        "fields": [],
        "citations": [],
        "sources": [
          "rules"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "K21",
        "text": "Do not join tables not referenced in the question to avoid inadvertently filtering out investors without child records.",
        "fields": [],
        "citations": [],
        "sources": [
          "rules"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "K22",
        "text": "When combining optional child metrics, use LEFT JOIN from INVESTOR_PROFILE to ensure no cohort members are dropped.",
        "fields": [],
        "citations": [],
        "sources": [
          "rules"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "K23",
        "text": "Allocation concentration for an investor is defined as the largest single-sector share (MAX(allocation_pct)). For cohorts, compute per-investor MAX, then average across investors.",
        "fields": [
          {
            "table": "ATOM_ENTITY_SECTOR_ALLOCATION_001",
            "column": "allocation_pct"
          }
        ],
        "citations": [],
        "sources": [
          "rules"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "K24",
        "text": "risk_pressure_score = RS + (100 - LS) + (100 - DS), where RS=risk_score, LS=liquidity_score, DS=diversification_score. Investors with any NULL health score are excluded.",
        "fields": [
          {
            "table": "ATOM_ENTITY_PORTFOLIO_HEALTH_001",
            "column": "risk_score"
          },
          {
            "table": "ATOM_ENTITY_PORTFOLIO_HEALTH_001",
            "column": "liquidity_score"
          },
          {
            "table": "ATOM_ENTITY_PORTFOLIO_HEALTH_001",
            "column": "diversification_score"
          }
        ],
        "citations": [],
        "sources": [
          "rules"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "K25",
        "text": "quantitative_burden_index is a normalized 0\u2013100 index of {SHORT, \u2212GAIN, \u2212NCF, C1}, where components are min-max scaled to [0,1] and then averaged. C1 = risk_pressure_score.",
        "fields": [
          {
            "table": "ATOM_ENTITY_INVESTMENT_GOAL_001",
            "column": "shortfall"
          },
          {
            "table": "ATOM_ENTITY_PORTFOLIO_HOLDING_001",
            "column": "current_value"
          },
          {
            "table": "ATOM_ENTITY_PORTFOLIO_HOLDING_001",
            "column": "cost"
          },
          {
            "table": "ATOM_EVENT_CASH_FLOW_001",
            "column": "amount"
          }
        ],
        "citations": [],
        "sources": [
          "rules"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "K26",
        "text": "combined_gain_and_ncf = GAIN + NCF, where GAIN = SUM(current_value \u2212 cost) and NCF = SUM(amount) over the specified period.",
        "fields": [
          {
            "table": "ATOM_ENTITY_PORTFOLIO_HOLDING_001",
            "column": "current_value"
          },
          {
            "table": "ATOM_ENTITY_PORTFOLIO_HOLDING_001",
            "column": "cost"
          },
          {
            "table": "ATOM_EVENT_CASH_FLOW_001",
            "column": "amount"
          }
        ],
        "citations": [],
        "sources": [
          "rules"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "K27",
        "text": "combined_ncf_and_reb = NCF + REB, where NCF = SUM(amount) from cash flows and REB = SUM(amount) from rebalancing actions.",
        "fields": [
          {
            "table": "ATOM_EVENT_CASH_FLOW_001",
            "column": "amount"
          },
          {
            "table": "ATOM_EVENT_REBALANCING_ACTION_001",
            "column": "amount"
          }
        ],
        "citations": [],
        "sources": [
          "rules"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "K28",
        "text": "combined_holding_value_and_shortfall = HVAL + SHORT, where HVAL = SUM(current_value) and SHORT = SUM(shortfall).",
        "fields": [
          {
            "table": "ATOM_ENTITY_PORTFOLIO_HOLDING_001",
            "column": "current_value"
          },
          {
            "table": "ATOM_ENTITY_INVESTMENT_GOAL_001",
            "column": "shortfall"
          }
        ],
        "citations": [],
        "sources": [
          "rules"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "K29",
        "text": "transaction_rebalance_index is a normalized 0\u2013100 index of {NCF, REB, SCEN\u0394sum}, where components are min-max scaled to [0,1] and then averaged.",
        "fields": [
          {
            "table": "ATOM_EVENT_CASH_FLOW_001",
            "column": "amount"
          },
          {
            "table": "ATOM_EVENT_REBALANCING_ACTION_001",
            "column": "amount"
          },
          {
            "table": "ATOM_EVENT_SCENARIO_REBALANCING_001",
            "column": "new_allocation_pct"
          },
          {
            "table": "ATOM_EVENT_SCENARIO_REBALANCING_001",
            "column": "current_allocation_pct"
          }
        ],
        "citations": [],
        "sources": [
          "rules"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "K30",
        "text": "temporal_pressure_index is a normalized 0\u2013100 index of {NCF(period), REB, \u2212AVGSHORT, SCEN\u0394sum}, where components are min-max scaled to [0,1] and then averaged. NCF period must be explicitly stated in the question.",
        "fields": [
          {
            "table": "ATOM_EVENT_CASH_FLOW_001",
            "column": "amount"
          },
          {
            "table": "ATOM_EVENT_REBALANCING_ACTION_001",
            "column": "amount"
          },
          {
            "table": "ATOM_ENTITY_INVESTMENT_GOAL_001",
            "column": "shortfall"
          },
          {
            "table": "ATOM_EVENT_SCENARIO_REBALANCING_001",
            "column": "new_allocation_pct"
          },
          {
            "table": "ATOM_EVENT_SCENARIO_REBALANCING_001",
            "column": "current_allocation_pct"
